      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BEE MY LOVER (4) has joined the Jackson Painting yard since she was last seen at Newcastle eight weeks ago. Has been tackling stronger races of late so looks nicely placed. Could kick off for the new stable with a win. DANCINGONSTARLIGHT (10) led last time out and stuck on for fourth in a decent performance at this circuit and distance, beaten 5 metres. Draws on the back row but with even luck her recent form is good enough to put her right in the finish. BOSS MAJOR (1) will find this easier than the last attempt. Led from this barrier two back at Charlton prior so can give a big sight. THE BANKER NZ (9) broke last time but won at Shepparton prior. Shouldn't spend a penny from this draw and the sprint lane may come in handy. Can bounce back.",
